_gate_spread":0.14660257449952546,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":73.3,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.8179672280863169,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.2747822172555332,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.3948980687813794,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.18656712629000716,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.22523808398984024,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.08961418891969575,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0014576590340624643,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":12.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.005600600501596276,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":43.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02297922825579586,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":61.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.01023,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Innoviva, Inc. operates as a biopharmaceutical company in the United States and internationally. Its royalty portfolio includes RELVAR/BREO ELLIPTA, a once-daily combination medicine consisting of a LABA, vilanterol, and an inhaled corticosteroid, and fluticasone furoate; ANORO ELLIPTA, a once-daily medicine combining a long-acting muscarinic antagonist, umeclidinium bromide, and ABA, VI. The company also markets GIAPREZA for increasing blood pressure in adults with septic or other distributive shock; XACDURO, a co-packaged for intravenous use for the treatment of hospital-acquired and ventilator-associated bacterial pneumonia caused by Acinetobacter; XERAVA for the treatment of complicated intra-abdominal infections in adults; ZEVTERA an advanced-generation cephalosporin antibiotic for the treatment of staphylococcus aureus bacteremia, as well as with right-sided endocarditis, acute bacterial skin and skin structure infections, and community-acquired bacterial pneumonia; NUZOLVENCE for the treatment of uncomplicated urogenital gonorrhea in adults and adolescents. In addition, the company develops bacteriophages with potential use in a range of infectious and other serious diseases. It has a strategic partnership with Sarissa Capital Management LP; and LABA Collaboration Agreement with Glaxo Group Limited to develop and commercialize once-daily products for the treatment of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and asthma. The company was formerly known as Theravance, Inc. and changed its name to Innoviva, Inc. in January 2016. Innoviva, Inc. was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in Burlingame, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Pavel  Raifeld C.F.A. | CEO & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 159 people. Revenue per employee of $2.6M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 22%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $1.2M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $59K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Innoviva, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.4B market cap on $411M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +23% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +34.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 75% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $196M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 48 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.73\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 9.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 4.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 39% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 80% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 64% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Innoviva (INVA) Stock Could Be Undervalued On Third Quarter Results","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-inva/innoviva/news/innoviva-inva-stock-could-be-undervalued-on-third-quarter-re","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793941010.481,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.969,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Innoviva (INVA) Could Be 39% Undervalued Following Third Quarter Loss","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-inva/innoviva/news/innoviva-inva-could-be-39-undervalued-following-third-quarte","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793850316.756,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Innoviva (INVA) Tops Q3 Earnings Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023673/innoviva-inva-tops-q3-earnings-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3023673","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793835913.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Innoviva (NASDAQ:INVA) and Shionogi & Co., Ltd. Unsponsored ADR (OTCMKTS:SGIOY) Head to Head Review","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolniano